From: buntOS contributors
Subject: [PATCH] soc: mediatek: add the MT6897 video coprocessor

The VCP of the MT6897 is a RISC-V core that runs the video codec firmware:
the firmware parses the bitstreams and drives the decoder hardware. The
bootloader loads it and maps it for the coprocessor. This driver powers
the core, hands it a window of shared memory, has the secure monitor
release the reset and waits for the ready message. A user of the firmware
starts the coprocessor through this driver and exchanges messages with it;
the messages live in fixed slots of five mailboxes.

The sequence, the registers, the layout of the mailboxes and the log
protocol are those of the MediaTek driver in the OnePlus MT6897 kernel
(drivers/misc/mediatek/vcp/rv). The shape follows the VCP driver of the
MT6895-Mainline tree. Recovery after a watchdog, dumps and the sleep
votes of the vendor driver are left out.

Until a decoder uses it, debugfs has a switch to start the coprocessor
(mt6897-vcp/hold), its state and the log of the firmware.
---
 drivers/soc/mediatek/Kconfig            |   11 +
 drivers/soc/mediatek/Makefile           |    1 +
 drivers/soc/mediatek/mt6897-vcp.c       | 1002 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 include/linux/soc/mediatek/mt6897-vcp.h |   86 +++
 4 files changed, 1100 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/soc/mediatek/Kconfig b/drivers/soc/mediatek/Kconfig
index ee64834b5..7289a9c56 100644
--- a/drivers/soc/mediatek/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/soc/mediatek/Kconfig
@@ -102,6 +102,17 @@ config MTK_SVS
 	  chip process corner, temperatures and other factors. Then DVFS
 	  driver could apply SVS bank voltage to PMIC/Buck.
 
+config MTK_MT6897_VCP
+	tristate "MediaTek MT6897 video coprocessor"
+	depends on ARCH_MEDIATEK || COMPILE_TEST
+	depends on HAVE_ARM_SMCCC && IOMMU_API && OF
+	help
+	  Say y or m here for the video coprocessor (VCP) of the MT6897: a
+	  RISC-V core that runs the video codec firmware. The bootloader
+	  loads the firmware. This driver powers the core, has the secure
+	  monitor release its reset and carries the messages between the
+	  firmware and its users, such as the video decoder.
+
 config MTK_SOCINFO
 	tristate "MediaTek SoC Information"
 	default y
diff --git a/drivers/soc/mediatek/Makefile b/drivers/soc/mediatek/Makefile
index 31c625860..cae099609 100644
